wlanpi-bluetooth (1.0.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * bt-agent/bt-network: lazy-load from bluetooth.target instead of
    multi-user.target so they start only once the controller exists and BlueZ
    is up. Starting at multi-user made bt-agent block ~25s on BlueZ's D-Bus
    and abort (intf_supported assertion), and delayed multi-user.target,
    because bluetooth.service is condition-skipped until the hci device
    appears. bt-network likewise died immediately.
  * bt-agent/bt-network: unblock the soft-blocked adapter
    (rfkill.default_state=0) with "rfkill unblock bluetooth" in ExecStartPre.
    Without it, bt-adapter --set Powered fails with org.bluez.Error.Failed on
    USB Bluetooth adapters (for example the M4+ Intel BE200), which the
    on-board rfkill whitelist does not cover.
  * bt-agent: retry power restoration while BlueZ transitions the adapter out
    of rfkill, and run bt-agent directly so systemd tracks the real process.
    Stop it directly because bluez-tools can hang indefinitely while
    unregistering its agent over D-Bus.
  * Migrate existing enablement links from multi-user.target to
    bluetooth.target during package upgrades.

 -- Josh Schmelzle <josh@joshschmelzle.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:30:00 -0400

wlanpi-bluetooth (1.0.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Move avahi configuration from preinst to postinst: preinst runs at
    unpack before dependencies exist, which failed the trixie image
    build when avahi-daemon was not yet installed
  * Guard the avahi edits on the conffile existing and drop sudo
  * Depend on avahi-daemon so configure ordering is guaranteed

